#
# Allow-list for ios/Vauchi/Views/*.swift consumed by
# scripts/scripts/check-domain-named-views.sh (wired into `just lint ios`).
#
# Ratchet-down: each retirement MR (problem record
# 2026-05-02-ios-humble-ui-deep-retirement, G1) deletes both the view
# file and its entry below. The destination is the platform-required
# subset only.
#
# One filename per line. Lines starting with `#` and blank lines
# ignored.
#
# --- Platform-required / kept (permanent) ----------------------------
# LockScreenView    — pre-unlock biometric host; runs before core is
#                     decrypted, so cannot render a core ScreenModel.
# AppPasswordView   — pre-unlock password entry; same constraint.
# QRScannerView     — AVCaptureSession host (camera lifecycle owner).
# WaitingForUnlockView — pre-unlock wait state; same constraint.
# QRDiagnosticView  — `#if DEBUG`-only diagnostic that intentionally
#                     exercises the FFI layer (MobileQrEccLevel) to tune
#                     the multi-stage exchange protocol. Active dev tool,
#                     not a retirement target (G8 of the problem record).
# AVCameraCaptureSheet lives in CoreUI/, out of scope for this lint.
AppPasswordView.swift
LockScreenView.swift
QRScannerView.swift
WaitingForUnlockView.swift
QRDiagnosticView.swift

# --- To-be-retired (G1 targets) --------------------------------------
# Empty: G1 complete 2026-06-06. The last two domain-named shells
# (FaceToFaceExchangeView + NfcTapExchangeView) were byte-identical
# render-only wrappers differing only by screen-id guard; unified into the
# non-domain-named `CoreUI/ExchangeHardwareScreen` (out of this lint's
# Views/ scope). QRDiagnosticView reclassified as a kept dev tool (above)
# per G8. Any NEW domain-named view in Views/ is now rejected by the lint.
